 Nautilus Custom Apache Docker Image
Overview
This document outlines the requirements and implementation details for creating a custom Apache Docker image for Project Nautilus on Application Server 3 (stapp03).

Task Requirements
Target Server: Application Server 3 (stapp03) in Stratos DC.

File Path: /opt/docker/Dockerfile (Ensure strict capitalization: capital D in Dockerfile).

Base Image: ubuntu:24.04

Web Server: Install apache2 and configure it to listen on port 8088 (without altering other Apache default configurations like document root).

Dockerfile Implementation
The following configuration is placed inside /opt/docker/Dockerfile:

Dockerfile
FROM ubuntu:24.04

ENV DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive

RUN apt-get update && \
    apt-get install -y apache2 && \
    apt-get clean && \
    rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

RUN sed -i 's/80/8088/g' /etc/apache2/ports.conf && \
    sed -i 's/:80/:8088/g' /etc/apache2/sites-available/000-default.conf

EXPOSE 8088

CMD ["apache2ctl", "-D", "FOREGROUND"]
Build and Run Instructions
1. Build the Docker Image
Navigate to the directory containing the Dockerfile and build the image:

Bash
cd /opt/docker
sudo docker build -t nautilus-apache:latest .
2. Run the Container
Start a container from the custom image, mapping port 8088:

Bash
sudo docker run -d -p 8088:8088 --name test-apache nautilus-apache:latest
3. Verify Container Status
Check that the container is up and running correctly:

Bash
sudo docker ps
4. Test the Endpoint
Verify that Apache responds successfully on port 8088:

Bash
curl http://localhost:8088
